 "title": "The lab's first session: the jab string, the pass, and the lift turned off",
 "human": {
  "said_on": "2026-11-23",
  "said": [
   "wow this is getting fucking cool. Couldn't get through all the knobs.",
   "what i feel is getting better is understanding the subcontext of each held chord. these are typically shoulders, and one held action, so three.",
   "I found you can hot pass to the command button and then pump the previous held action. so you get a heavy hit then gun shots if you were holding gun.",
   "The gun needs to be always held in ready position if the gun button is held.",
   "The melee needs to feel like the movement of the enemy is enough so that jabs can follow for at least 4 hits. the fifth should miss and the forth is a right jab.",
   "the first jab special is left cross, second is right uppercut, the third is the haymaker. the forth can be strung to a new combo, if special is hit after it's a jab.",
   "With the camera tracking the juggled enemy."
  ],
